  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="transcription" xml:id="transcription_aad_0172" xml:lang="en">
          <div type="letter">
        <pb facs="https://iiif.acdh.oeaw.ac.at/aad/aad_00517/" ed="1r" type="sheet"/>
            <div type="letter_message" hand="#type_black_gardner">
              <opener>
                <seg hand="#print_gardner">
                  <placeName>
                    <address>
                      <lb/><rs type="place" ref="#amp_place_id_567">10 LYNTON ROAD
                      <lb/>NEW MALDEN
                      <lb/>SURREY
                      <lb/>KT3 5EE</rs>
                    </address>
                  </placeName>
                    <lb/>01-942 7322
                </seg>
                <dateline>  
                  <date>
                    <lb/><space quantity="26" unit="char"/>22-ix-73
                  </date>
                </dateline>
                <salute>
                  <lb/>Dear <rs type="person" ref="#amp_person_1">Mr Auden</rs>,
                </salute>
              </opener>
              <p>
                <lb/><space quantity="6" unit="char"/>Splendid news about the <rs type="lit_work" ref="#lit_work_id_407">Anti-Masque</rs>, and I thoroughly
                <lb/>approve of your idea to insert it in the <rs type="lit_work" ref="#lit_work_id_404">Masque</rs>, where an
                <lb/>Anti-Masque should properly be.
              </p>
              <p>
                <lb/><space quantity="6" unit="char"/>I note you'll be back on 4 October, and have apprised
                <lb/>the <rs ana="#ana_148">producer David William of the fact, so that you, he and
                <lb/>I may have an early meeting; possibly also with the conduct-
                <lb/>or <rs type="person" ref="#amp_person_563">John Eliot Gardiner</rs></rs>, son of <rs type="person" ref="#amp_person_564">Rolf</rs>, whom you must have known
                <lb/>(and p<subst><del rend="overtyped" hand="#type_black_gardner">o</del><add place="superimposed" hand="#type_black_gardner">r</add></subst>obably disapproved of) in the thirties.<space quantity="2" unit="char"/>Now dead, of
                <lb/>course; dramatically and unexpectedly, of a pulmonary throm-
                <lb/>bosis, a couple of years or so ago.
              </p>
              <p>
                <lb/><space quantity="6" unit="char"/>My opera for children <rs type="lit_work" ref="#lit_work_id_405">"Bel and the D<subst><del rend="overwritten" hand="#hand_black_gardner">ar</del><add place="superimposed" hand="#hand_black_gardner">r<unclear>a</unclear></add></subst>gon"</rs> is complete
                <lb/>in vocal score; I still have to finish the full score, but
                <lb/>expect that to take me about to the date of your return, af-
                <lb/>ter which it will be all hands to work on<rs type="lit_work" ref="#lit_work_id_181"><add hand="#hand_black_gardner" place="above">your</add> Cupid</rs>.
              </p>
              <p>
                <lb/><space quantity="6" unit="char"/>I have to be in <rs type="place" ref="#amp_place_id_46">Oxford</rs> on 4 November, when I direc<subst><del rend="overwritten" hand="#hand_black_gardner">y</del><add place="superimposed" hand="#hand_black_gardner">t</add></subst> a
                <lb/>performance at the <rs type="place" ref="#amp_place_id_569">Sheldonian</rs> of my <rs type="lit_work" ref="#lit_work_id_406">Seven Songs</rs>, as the fin-
                <lb/>ale of a concert which celebrates fifty years of <rs type="org" ref="#amp_organization_69">O.U.P.</rs> Music
                <lb/>Publishing.<space quantity="2" unit="char"/>It would be nice if you would come to that.<space quantity="2" unit="char"/>Fur-
                <lb/>thermore I shall be hanging around Oxford from Friday aftern<subst><del rend="overtyped" hand="#type_black_gardner">n</del><add place="superimposed" hand="#type_black_gardner">o</add></subst><add hand="#hand_black_gardner" place="inline">on</add>
                <lb/>through Sunday and could confer with you perhaps during that
                <lb/>time.<space quantity="2" unit="char"/>I should have written something by then.
              </p>
              <p>
                <lb/><space quantity="6" unit="char"/>The <rs type="org" ref="#amp_organization_366">Arts Council</rs> tr<subst><del rend="overtyped" hand="#type_black_gardner">w</del><add place="superimposed" hand="#type_black_gardner">e</add></subst>ated me similarly to you.<space quantity="2" unit="char"/>But this
                <lb/>of course is a mere '<foreign xml:lang="fr">douceur</foreign>'; it has nothing to do with
                <lb/>perf<subst><del rend="overwritten" hand="#hand_black_gardner">ro</del><add place="superimposed" hand="#hand_black_gardner">or</add></subst>ming rights, royalites or any ag<del rend="overstrike" hand="#hand_black_gardner">g</del>reement you care to
                <lb/>make with my <rs type="org" ref="#amp_organization_69">publishers</rs> or me with your <rs type="org" ref="#amp_organization_29">agents</rs>.<space quantity="2" unit="char"/>It doesn't
                <lb/>even have to be treated as taxable income (I have a letter
                <lb/>from the <rs type="org" ref="#amp_organization_366">A.C.</rs> to this effect!<subst><del rend="overtyped" hand="#type_black_gardner">I</del><add place="superimposed" hand="#type_black_gardner">)</add></subst>.
              </p>
              <closer>
                <salute>
                  <lb/><space quantity="22" unit="char"/>Yours sincerely,
                </salute>
                <signed hand="#hand_black_gardner">
                  <lb/><rs type="person" ref="#amp_person_561">John Gardner</rs>
                </signed>
              </closer>
             </div>
        <pb facs="https://iiif.acdh.oeaw.ac.at/aad/aad_00518/" ed="1v" type="sheet"/>
            <div>
              <ab hand="#hand_blue_unident_0172">
                <lb/>68
              </ab>
            </div>
          </div>
      </div>
